"learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Short O Sound", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The vowels in our alphabet are A, E, I, O, and U. The other  letters are called consonants. </br>The vowels can be a short sound such as log, or a long vowel sound such as lone.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "dog, log, socks, off, on, and  top", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you  say the o sound, your mouth must be open.</br> Your lips should NOT be rounded with the tongue low and relaxed.</br>Most of the time, the short O sound comes in the middle of a word like <span class=\"italic\"> pot</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> fog</span> .", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Demonstrative Adjectives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Some demonstrative adjectives are <span class=\"italic\"> this</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> these</span>. You use them to point out specific people or things.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> This</span> is used to point out something close by. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> These</span> is used to point out things close by. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This bike is red.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Look at these shoes and clothes.", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Use the words <span class=\"italic\">jog</span>, <span class=\"italic\">walk</span>, <span class=\"italic\">o'clock</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">top</span> from the dialogue to make 4 sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the sentences aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare your sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Can you say this tongue twister fast 5 times? <br/><span class=\"italic\">Bob's shop sells spotted socks.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content":